From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Subject: [PATCH] libzip: include unistd.h on POSIX, not just Apple and Switch

_zip_create_temp_output() calls close(), but unistd.h is included only for
__APPLE__ and __SWITCH__. Every other POSIX target relied on the compiler
implicitly declaring it, which GCC 14 turned from a warning into an error in
all C modes - so -std=gnu17 does not bring it back.

--- a/core/deps/libzip/zip_close.c
+++ b/core/deps/libzip/zip_close.c
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
 
 #include "zipint.h"
 
-#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__SWITCH__)
+#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__SWITCH__) || defined(__unix__)
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
 
